<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>出版物 |皮尤研究中心</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/publications/</link><description>塑造您世界的数字、事实和趋势</description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 05:25:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>美国人使用社交媒体获取健康信息的情况因种族和民族而异</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/13/americans-use-of-social-media-for-health-information-differs-by-race-and-ethnicity/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.13_health-info_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;西班牙裔、黑人和亚裔成年人比白人成年人更有可能从社交媒体获取健康信息，并向健康和健康影响者寻求帮助。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:57:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/13/americans-use-of-social-media-for-health-information-differs-by-race-and-ethnicity/</guid></item><item><title>印度和巴基斯坦：对全球秩序持有不同看法的对手</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/08/13/india-and-pakistan-rivals-with-divergent-views-of-the-global-order/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/PG_26.08.12_IndiaPakistan_featured@2x.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;印度人和巴基斯坦人倾向于将对方国家视为最大威胁，双方都怀疑对方对良好关系的承诺。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:57:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/08/13/india-and-pakistan-rivals-with-divergent-views-of-the-global-order/</guid></item><item><title>36个国家对印度的舆论褒贬不一</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/13/public-opinion-of-india-is-mixed-across-36-countries/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.13_views-of-india_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;印度36个国家的民意差异很大，支持率从斯里兰卡的79%到巴基斯坦的7%不等。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:57:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/13/public-opinion-of-india-is-mixed-across-36-countries/</guid></item><item><title>特朗普第二届政府结束了大多数拥有临时保护身份的移民的临时保护身份</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/12/second-trump-administration-has-ended-temporary-protected-status-for-most-immigrants-who-had-it/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.12_TPS_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;特朗普第二届政府终止了 13 个国家的临时保护地位，影响了约 100 万受益人。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:57:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/12/second-trump-administration-has-ended-temporary-protected-status-for-most-immigrants-who-had-it/</guid></item><item><title>大多数美国成年人在 40 岁出头时就已与尚未结婚的浪漫伴侣同居</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/12/most-us-adults-have-lived-with-a-romantic-partner-theyre-not-married-to-by-their-early-40s/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.12_Cohabitation_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;大约四分之三的 30 岁末或 40 岁出头的美国人曾与他们一生中某个阶段未结婚的浪漫伴侣住在一起。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:57:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/12/most-us-adults-have-lived-with-a-romantic-partner-theyre-not-married-to-by-their-early-40s/</guid></item></channel></rss>